    "final_answer": "I have found the perfect beginner-level Python course on Coursera. Here is my final answer:\n\n## Recommended Beginner Python Course\n\n**Course Title:** Programming for Everybody (Getting Started with Python) / 人人都会编程（Python 入门）\n\n**Key Details:**\n- **Provider:** University of Michigan\n- **Instructor:** Charles Russell Severance\n- **Level:** Beginner — **No prior experience required** (无需具备相关经验)\n- **Rating:** 4.8/5 stars (233,721 reviews)\n- **Enrolled Students:** 3,642,264\n- **Duration:** 7 modules (Flexible schedule, self-paced)\n- **Cost:** Free to enroll (starts September 25)\n- **Language:** English (with 27 language options including Chinese Simplified)\n- **Assignments:** 9 tasks\n- **Student Recommendation Rate:** 98%\n\n**What you'll learn:**\n- Install Python and write your first program\n- Describe the basics of the Python programming language\n- Use variables to store, retrieve, and compute data\n\n**Skills you'll gain:**\n- Programming Principles\n- Software Installation\n- Computer Programming\n- Debugging\n\n**Note:** This course is the first course in the popular \"Python for Everybody\" Specialization by the University of Michigan. If you'd like to continue learning, the full Specialization has 280K+ reviews and a 4.8 rating, and takes about 3-6 months to complete.\n\n**Direct Course Link:** https://www.coursera.org/learn/python\n\nThis is widely considered one of the best beginner Python courses on Coursera, especially for complete beginners, because the instructor Charles Severance explains concepts in a very accessible way, and the course assumes no prior programming knowledge.",
